Source: https://www.whatdotheyknow.com/request/bsc_mathematics_part_a_examinati/response/2820674/attach/3/FOI%20202410%20944%20Data.pdf#page=135[Oxford Part A, A7 Numerical Analysis, A13759W1, 23 June 2023; parent PDF pages 135–137, paper pages 1–3]. These original solutions cover all three questions and all eleven lettered subparts. In Question 1(d), the unrefined <Gershgorin discs> alone are inconclusive for the shift $5$; a further exact calculation resolves it. In Question 2(c), clearing denominators produces a <linear system> whose solution need not define a <rational interpolant> at every <interpolation node>. Question 3 uses the paper's normalized convention for the <local truncation error>.

